{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, user_id 8, America/Chicago, hours 06:00-14:00) says his warehouse office desktop BL-DT-0108 won't connect to the network. His shift starts in about an hour, so he is blocked (P2). Checked: account is active, not locked or blocked, VPN access is on. Device status shows BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro desktop) OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11 00:59 UTC, 78% disk free, no warnings. Not known yet: whether it's wired or Wi-Fi, and whether other warehouse office devices or colleagues are affected. If several people are down, treat it as a site outage and raise the priority. KB-014 only partly fits because it's written for laptops on Wi-Fi. No KB covers a wired desktop, and Tier 1 tools can't fix this remotely. I asked the user to restart, reseat the network cable, and check whether colleagues are affected. Still needed: on-site or network checks (switch port/patch, NIC, DHCP), and possibly a loaner PC if it isn't fixed before his shift.",
  "reason": "Desktop offline, user blocked before shift, no KB covers wired desktop connectivity, can't be fixed with Tier 1 tools"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked your warehouse office desktop. It isn't reaching our network right now; it last connected late yesterday evening. Your account is fine, so this is a connection problem, not a login problem. Because your shift starts soon, I've passed this to our Tier 2 team as urgent, and they'll follow up with you. While you wait, a few quick things to try: (1) Fully restart the PC. (2) If it uses a network cable, make sure both ends are pushed in firmly, at the back of the PC and at the wall or desk port. Check whether the light next to the port on the PC is on. (3) If it uses Wi-Fi, turn Wi-Fi off and back on. (4) Ask colleagues nearby whether their computers are online. If several people are offline, please reply and tell us right away so we can treat it as an office-wide problem. If any of these steps fixes it, just reply and let us know.",
  "internal_note": "BL-DT-0108 (James O'Connor, user_id 8) shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 00:59 UTC. 78% disk free, no warnings. Account is active, not locked or sign-in blocked, VPN access is on. KB-014 only partly applies because it's written for laptops on Wi-Fi. No KB covers a wired desktop, so I escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) as P2 since the user is blocked and his shift starts in about 1 hour. I asked the user to restart, reseat the cable, and check whether colleagues are affected. If several are, raise to a site outage. Next steps may be on-site checks (switch port, patch, NIC, DHCP) or a loaner PC.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
